# Who is asked to look at a change, by the part of the repository it touches.
#
# A country pack is the one thing here that nobody can review from the code:
# a rate, a box or a chart is right or wrong against a law, and the person who
# knows is the person who applies it. So every pack has an owner, and a pull
# request that moves one asks them before it moves.
#
# Ownership is not certification. `@Ekwo-ai/maintainers` maintains Belgium and
# France — `certification.status` says `maintained`, not `reviewed`, and it
# will keep saying that until a named professional has read the pack and put
# their name in the manifest. A pack a contributor owns is listed below with
# their handle, and its status is `community` until the same thing happens.

# `@Ekwo-ai/maintainers` is a team of the organisation. Until it exists and has
# write access, GitHub requests no review from these lines and reports them as
# unknown owners; the file is valid either way, and the day the team is created
# every line below starts working without an edit.

# Everything, unless a line below is more specific.
*                       @Ekwo-ai/maintainers

# The schema every pack is validated against. A change here changes what every
# country may say, so it is deliberately not owned by one pack's owner.
/packs/schema/          @Ekwo-ai/maintainers

# One line per pack.
/packs/be/              @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
/packs/ee/              @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
/packs/fr/              @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
/packs/lu/              @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
/packs/generic/         @Ekwo-ai/maintainers

# The compiled seeds are a build artefact of the packs above; they move with
# them and are read by the same people.
/supabase/seed/         @Ekwo-ai/maintainers

# The ledger and what the law does to it: migrations, the pack reader and the
# compiler, the golden runner.
/supabase/migrations/   @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
/packages/cli/src/pack/ @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
/tests/golden.test.ts   @Ekwo-ai/maintainers
